{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>From there HaShem scattered them.</b> This teaches that they have no share in the World to Come. And which was harsher — the generation of the Flood or the generation of the Dispersion? These did not stretch out their hand against the Essence, while those stretched out their hand against the Essence to fight against Him; yet these were swept away while those were not destroyed from the world? Rather, the generation of the Flood were robbers and there was strife among them — therefore they were destroyed. But these conducted themselves with love and fellowship among themselves, as it says: ״שָׂפָה אֶחָת וּדְבָרִים אֲחָדִים״ — you have learned that discord is hateful and peace is great."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:19.308041026Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}